# Normalize line endings; keep binaries untouched.
#
# `eol=lf` is deliberate and it is the whole policy: LF in the index and LF in
# the working tree, on every platform. If you also have `core.autocrlf=true` set
# globally — Git for Windows offers it during installation, so many people do —
# the two disagree, and Git reports files as permanently modified with an empty
# diff, because the blob it hashes matches while the stat check never settles.
# Nothing is actually wrong with those files. Turn it off for this repository:
#
#     git config --local core.autocrlf false
#
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff2 binary
